      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Lassiter Lumber Company, founded in Cullomburg in 1912, hauled pine lumber by mule and shipped it by rail.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/cullomburg_alabama",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Cullomburg sits within the Tombigbee River watershed, where bottomland hardwoods and creeks shape local flood patterns.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/cullomburg_alabama",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "During the April 12, 2020 tornado outbreak, straight‑line winds of 60–80 mph struck Cullomburg, damaging trees but sparing lives.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/cullomburg_alabama",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Cullomburg enjoys a humid subtropical climate, with July highs around 92°F, January lows near 36°F, and about 58 inches of rain yearly.",
